      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the Provider**\n\nI'm starting to sketch out the `query_error_logs.py` script. The key is to get a handle on logging, and I've decided to concentrate on Google Cloud Logging. I will embed this provider as a primary requirement. Now, I will start to implement the filters for severity and timeframe.\n\n\n**Implementing the Client**\n\nI've decided to move forward with the Python code itself. I'm focusing on the concrete steps. I'll import classes from `google.cloud.logging_v2`, and initialize a logging client. I'll define a function that will take severity and time range. From there I'll construct the filter string. I have started the implementation using the `google-cloud-logging` library, and the comments will identify the provider. Now, I will use a `write` tool to create the file.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789819605404,
          "start": 1789819601207
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b98fc1370018YGvPLLZ5mHQRL",
      "message_id": "msg_0b98fbc100010mYikeHZ42yaNs",
      "session_id": "ses_f4670440dffeH5YZcBRpgnIwpr",
      "time_created": 1789819601207,
